msgid "List payment methods"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:742
msgid "List every individual payment method offered by a payment service (ECPay, NewebPay, PAYUNi, SmilePay, PayNow or PChomePay) and whether each is enabled. Use it to confirm what is available before switching anything. Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:749
#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:789
msgid "The payment service name or slug, for example ECPay or ecpay"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:781
msgid "Enable or disable payment methods"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:782
msgid "Enable or disable one or more individual payment methods within a payment service, such as ECPay's one-off credit card payment, Apple Pay or ATM. Pass the method names directly. This is a destructive action — calling the tool only proposes it, and nothing takes effect until the user presses Confirm, so there is no need to ask for confirmation yourself."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:794
msgid "An array of payment method names, for example [\"Credit card, pay in full\",\"Apple Pay\"]"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:832
msgid "Issue an invoice allowance"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:833
msgid "Issue an allowance against an order's existing e-invoice, used for partial refunds. An amount is required. Only ECPay, ezPay and Amego support this. It is destructive and cannot be undone — calling the tool only proposes it, and nothing is issued until the user presses Confirm, so there is no need to ask for confirmation yourself."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:844
msgid "The allowance amount as a whole number, which cannot exceed the order total"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:876
msgid "Advanced order list"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:877
msgid "Return an actual list of orders, filtered by status, date range (date_from and date_to in YYYY-MM-DD format) and payment method. The list is compact and returns 20 orders by default, up to a maximum of 50. If you only need counts per status, use query-orders instead. Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:884
msgid "An order status slug such as processing or completed. Omit it for every status"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:888
msgid "Start date in YYYY-MM-DD format"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:892
msgid "End date in YYYY-MM-DD format"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:896
msgid "Payment method ID (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:900
msgid "How many orders to return. Defaults to 20, maximum 50"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:937
msgid "List payment, shipping and e-invoice channels"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:938
msgid "List the payment, shipping and e-invoice channels with their slugs and whether each is enabled. Use all for everything, or filter with payment, shipping or invoice. Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:947
msgid "Optional, defaults to all. Or filter with payment, shipping or invoice"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:979
msgid "Enable or disable a channel"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:980
msgid "Enable or disable a payment, shipping or e-invoice channel. Pass the channel name (such as “SmilePay shipping”) or its slug directly; there is no need to list them first. This is a destructive action, because disabling a channel changes what customers can choose at checkout and enabling one without credentials causes errors on the storefront — calling the tool only proposes it, and nothing takes effect until the user presses Confirm, so there is no need to ask for confirmation yourself. It does not touch credentials or the test and production switch."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:987
msgid "The channel name or slug, for example “SmilePay shipping” or smilepay_shipping"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:1023
msgid "Add an invoice donation charity"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:1024
msgid "Add a charity, with its name and love code, to the donation list of the enabled e-invoice module so customers can choose it at checkout. A love code is 3 to 7 digits. Calling the tool only proposes it, and nothing is saved until the user presses Confirm, so there is no need to ask for confirmation yourself."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:1031
msgid "The name of the charity"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:1035
msgid "The love code, 3 to 7 digits"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:1069
msgid "Create a shipment"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:1070
msgid "Create a shipment with the carrier for an order and get its tracking number, choosing the carrier automatically from the order's shipping method. This is destructive and cannot be undone, because it places a real booking with the carrier — calling the tool only proposes it, and nothing is created until the user presses Confirm, so there is no need to ask for confirmation yourself. A label can only be printed once the shipment exists."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:1111
msgid "Look the payment up at the provider"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:1112
msgid "Ask the payment provider directly what happened to the transaction on an order — whether it was authorised, how much was captured and when. Use this when the order and the provider might disagree, for example when a customer says they paid but the order still shows unpaid. Works for ECPay card payments and PAYUNi. For what this site already recorded, use get-payment-status instead, which does not call the provider. Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:1156
msgid "List the shipments on an order"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:1157
msgid "List the shipments already created for an order, with their shipment numbers, tracking numbers and when they were created. Use this before deleting a shipment so you know which number to give."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:1199
msgid "Delete a shipment from an order"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:1200
msgid "Remove a shipment record from an order so the shipment can be created again — for example after the pickup store was changed. This only removes the record on this site; it does not cancel the booking with the carrier, so never use it for a parcel that is already on its way. This is a destructive action — calling the tool only proposes it, and nothing is deleted until the user presses Confirm, so there is no need to ask for confirmation yourself. If the order has more than one shipment you must say which shipment number to delete."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:1211
msgid "Which shipment to delete. Can be left out only when the order has exactly one shipment."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:1245
msgid "Change the pickup store"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:1246
msgid "Change which convenience store an order is picked up at, by store number. Use this when a customer asks to collect the parcel somewhere else. This is a destructive action — calling the tool only proposes the change, and nothing happens until the user presses Confirm, so there is no need to ask for confirmation yourself. It does not re-book the shipment: if a shipment was already created it still points at the old store and has to be deleted and created again on the order screen. If the store name and address are not given they are cleared, because keeping the old ones would show the new number next to the old store name."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:1257
msgid "The number of the store to switch to, for example 131386"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:1261
msgid "The store name, if the user gave one. Leave it out rather than guessing — a wrong name is worse than none."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:1265
msgid "The store address, if the user gave one. Leave it out rather than guessing."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:1299
msgid "Add an order note"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:1300
msgid "Add an internal note to an order. It is for your own records and is not sent to the customer."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:1311
msgid "The note"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/OrderLookup/Ability.php:1368
msgid "The note cannot be empty."
msgstr ""

